Craft 4K (apps/craft4k)

Game (engine/)
  Minecraft4k-CPP, by TheSunCat (RealTheSunCat) and contributors: a C++
  remake of Minecraft4k-Reversed, the decompiled and expanded version of
  Notch's Minecraft4k (2010), that ray-marches the world on the GPU.
  License: GNU General Public License version 3 (engine/LICENSE).
  Source: https://github.com/TheSunCat/Minecraft4k-CPP, commit
  cfb537a35c85ee18b01b4305fd975740f67f0380, with frunk.store's changes for
  the browser. The complete source of what's compiled, with the changes and
  the build script, is engine/craft4k-web-src.tar.gz; the changes are also
  tools/craft4k/ in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose
  tools/build-craft4k.mjs builds it.
  The changes: craft4k-web.patch uses the GLES 3 headers in place of glad,
  drops the GL debug callback, packs the texture atlas as RGBA and keeps the
  world generator inside the world; web.cpp replaces Minecraft4k.cpp and
  Shader.cpp with a front end for the page: the compute shader as a WebGL 2
  fragment shader (with a step limit, the pointed-at block outlined and
  square pixels on any screen), breaking and placing blocks, input, and the
  player's state and changes handed to the page to save.

  It includes GLM (OpenGL Mathematics) by G-Truc Creation, under the MIT
  license (engine/GLM-LICENSE.txt; include/glm/ in the source archive), and is compiled with Emscripten, whose runtime parts are under the
  MIT and University of Illinois/NCSA licenses.

